# Review routing. A path listed here needs an approval from its owner before a pull request merges —
# but only once branch protection is set to require review from Code Owners; the file alone requests
# a review and blocks nothing.
#
# `@sunnybai01` is a placeholder — one maintainer, standing in until a team exists. Replace it with a
# GitHub team that has write access, and note that GitHub does not error on a team that does not
# exist: it silently matches nobody and every rule below becomes decorative.
*                                   @sunnybai01

# The four surfaces SECURITY.md itself calls sensitive. Each is a place where a change that looks
# ordinary in review moves a trust boundary.

# The sandbox: the only unit that executes attacker-influenced code.
/services/builder/                  @sunnybai01

# Everything CI is permitted to do, and with what identity.
/.github/workflows/                 @sunnybai01

# What each service is allowed to read, and the `forbidden:` lists that hold ADR-002's line.
/config/                            @sunnybai01

# Applied migrations are content-hashed: editing one makes it read as modified on every live
# database that already ran it.
/packages/db/prisma/migrations/     @sunnybai01
/packages/db-query/prisma/migrations/ @sunnybai01

# The licence, the notices, and the two documents that state what this project promises.
/LICENSE                            @sunnybai01
/NOTICE                             @sunnybai01
/SECURITY.md                        @sunnybai01
/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md                 @sunnybai01
